{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1496590-dark-eras-content-for-mummy","id":1496590,"title":"Dark Eras content for Mummy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-09T06:25:24-08:00","id":1496590,"title":"Dark Eras content for Mummy","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Now that there is a second edition book, which content on the Dark Eras (1, 2, and Companion) is 2ed compatible? The Merits? (Interstitial Lives from DE is different from the one of the 2e Core book) The Affinities? Certainly the Utterances do not follow the 2e model.<br /> <br /> Another content that merits review is the crossover with Mage, specifically the artificial Vessels that Mages can create transferring Pillar points to a new object. Do these vestiges get their own Power, Curse, Virtue and Vice?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-09-2022, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T12:03:09-08:00","id":1496618,"title":"","content":"In terms of the eras themselves, they're all still relatively playable, but in terms of the mechanics...Maybe you could salvage some of the 1E Affinities, and of course the Crossover material of Princes of the Conquered Land is still applicable, but I would say the rest is probably best left alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T12:33:28-08:00","id":1496625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1496590-dark-eras-content-for-mummy?p=1496618#post1496618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of the eras themselves, they're all still relatively playable, but in terms of the mechanics...Maybe you could salvage some of the 1E Affinities, and of course the Crossover material of Princes of the Conquered Land is still applicable, but I would say the rest is probably best left alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer, what about the artificial Vessels that Mages can create transferring Pillar points to a new object. Do these vestiges get their own Power, Curse, Virtue and Vice?<br /> <br /> I am of the opinion that the vestige only stores specific Pillar points and that's it, that is why it is an &quot;artificial&quot; Vessel, in my opinion it should not have any qualities beyond what the text describes. But I would love to hear your rationale. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T12:36:45-08:00","id":1496626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1496590-dark-eras-content-for-mummy?p=1496625#post1496625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer, what about the artificial Vessels that Mages can create transferring Pillar points to a new object. Do these vestiges get their own Power, Curse, Virtue and Vice?<br /> <br /> I am of the opinion that the vestige only stores specific Pillar points and that's it, that is why it is an &quot;artificial&quot; Vessel, in my opinion it should not have any qualities beyond what the text describes. But I would love to hear your rationale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to reread a couple of things before giving a firm read, but on the off hand, I would lean more into Vessels made by Mages following the rules of 2nd Edition Curse, mostly because easy conversion and it maintains Mages' roles as being assholes who fuck up other people's ecosystems in their pursuits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-09-2022, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T13:05:06-08:00","id":1496631,"title":"","content":"The Prime Arcanum is not Sekhem. It can, at best, SIMULATE it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T13:25:45-08:00","id":1496633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1496590-dark-eras-content-for-mummy?p=1496631#post1496631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Prime Arcanum is not Sekhem. It can, at best, SIMULATE it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but this part was not being discussed.<br /> <br /> My point was that as described in the crossover section, mages create a very specific subset of Vessels, moving energy from an existing one to another object, and filling said object with Pillar points only. Since this is just specific pillars, I am of the opinion that it only stores said pillars as a battery and no further effects occur (no moving around pillars until you create the Vestige with the mechanical advantages you like).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T13:26:57-08:00","id":1496634,"title":"","content":"Ah! Ok! Objection withdrawn...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}